# How It Works

## Step 1 - Trigger Detection
Script polls the page every 2 seconds looking for 
a specific compliance warning box. When found, 
a one-click button is injected next to the 
existing UI buttons.

## Step 2 - Document Selection
Clicking the button opens the document modal, 
finds the correct templates by name, checks them, 
and clicks Add.

## Step 3 - Sequential Form Opening
After documents are added, the script uses 
sessionStorage flags to open each form Edit page 
one at a time across page navigations.

## Step 4 - Autofill
Each form script detects which form is open by 
page content, fills all fields including a 
dynamic daily date, then triggers the print flow.

## Step 5 - Print
More button is clicked, Print Document is selected, 
Chrome print dialog opens with the correct filename 
pre-filled (HS-105 or HS-118).
